          "address": "Bluetooth address"
        }
      },
      "reconfigure": {
        "title": "Change Bluetooth address",
        "description": "Change the Bluetooth address without losing the vehicle's paired key.",
        "data": {
          "address": "Bluetooth address"
        }
      },
      "vin": {
        "title": "Vehicle identification number",
        "description": "Enter the 17-character VIN of the vehicle at {address}. You can find it on the windshield, in the vehicle under Controls → Software, or on your registration.",
        "data": {
          "vin": "VIN"
        }
      },
      "pair": {
        "title": "Pair with your vehicle",
        "description": "Home Assistant needs its own key on the vehicle before it can send commands. Pairing installs the key, and the vehicle approves it when you tap a key card on the center console.\n\n1. Make sure the vehicle is awake and in Bluetooth range.\n2. Press **Submit**, then hold a key card against the center console.\n3. Confirm the key on the vehicle's touchscreen, then remove the card.\n\nIf pairing fails or the vehicle is not nearby right now, you can retry anytime with the **Pair** button on the vehicle's device page."
      }
    },
    "error": {
